   - Uses Railway GraphQL API (not CLI) for reliability
   - Monitors deployment status after trigger
   - Extracts and displays deployment URL
   - Posts deployment summary to GitHub Actions

   Key Implementation Details:
   - Uses serviceInstanceDeploy(latestCommit: true) not serviceInstanceRedeploy
   - This ensures fresh build from latest code, not cached image
   - Polls deployment status and extracts service URL via GraphQL
   - Requires 4 GitHub secrets: RAILWAY_TOKEN, RAILWAY_PROJECT_ID, RAILWAY_SERVICE_ID, RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_ID

   Design Decision: GraphQL API instead of Railway CLI
   - CLI requires interactive login, problematic in CI/CD
   - GraphQL API is stateless, token-based, more reliable
   - Provides better error handling and status monitoring
   - No dependency on @railway/cli package or version issues

